-- title:
--   Kneser's normal-subgroup step at a split place
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b$ be negative rationals, $\mathbb H=\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$, and let $\operatorname{nrd}(x)=x_0^2-ax_1^2-bx_2^2+abx_3^2$. Let $O\subseteq\mathbb H$ be a $\mathbb Z$-submodule that is an order in the sense of the project: $1\in O$, $O$ is closed under multiplication, its $\mathbb Q$-span is all of $\mathbb H$, and it is finitely generated. Let $v\neq w$ be primes of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$, and for a prime $w'$ write $\mathbb H_{w'}=\mathbb H\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_{w'}$ and let $\mathrm{localBox}\,O\,w'$ be the additive subgroup of $\mathbb H_{w'}$ generated by the elements $z\otimes c$ with $z\in O$ and $c$ in the valuation ring of $\mathbb Q_{w'}$. Call $t\in\mathbb H_w$ *of norm one* if $\operatorname{nrd}(\varphi(t))=1$ for every ring isomorphism $\varphi:\mathbb H_w\cong\mathbb H[\mathbb Q_w,a,b]$ satisfying $\varphi(z\otimes r)=r\cdot(z_0,z_1,z_2,z_3)$ coordinatewise, and *approximable* if for every $M\in\mathbb N$, $M\neq 0$, there is $\beta\in\mathbb H$ with $\operatorname{nrd}(\beta)=1$, with $\beta\otimes 1\in 1+M\cdot\mathrm{localBox}\,O\,w'$ for every prime $w'\notin\{v,w\}$, and with $\beta\otimes 1\in t+M\cdot\mathrm{localBox}\,O\,w$. Assume $\mathbb H_w$ contains a nonzero non-unit, and that some $s\in\mathbb H_w$ with $s\neq 1$, $s\neq-1$ is of norm one and approximable. Then every $s'\in\mathbb H_w$ of norm one is approximable.
--
--   This is the group-theoretic step in Kneser's proof of strong approximation for the norm-one group of a definite rational quaternion algebra, in the arrangement via $\mathrm{SL}_2$ of a split completion: the approximable norm-one elements form a normal subgroup of $\mathbb H_w^1\cong\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Q_w)$, so containing one non-central element forces it to be everything. It feeds the statements producing global norm-one elements with prescribed idelic behaviour, [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsOrder.exists_eq_finiteIdeleDiagonal_mul_mul_of_forall_nrd_eq_one`](thm.html#QuaternionAlgebra.IsOrder.exists_eq_finiteIdeleDiagonal_mul_mul_of_forall_nrd_eq_one) and [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsOrder.exists_nrd_eq_one_and_eq_finiteIdeleDiagonal_mul_mul_of_forall_nrd_eq_one`](thm.html#QuaternionAlgebra.IsOrder.exists_nrd_eq_one_and_eq_finiteIdeleDiagonal_mul_mul_of_forall_nrd_eq_one).
